<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_BeanLifecycle"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="authoring-agent" name="Authoring agent"/>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Agent bean lifecycle — folio-assistant
       Issue: https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/203

       BEANS ARE FOR AGENTS. They hold process state for work an agent
       is doing, in a store that is committed so a sibling session sees
       it. A human's own reminders are TODOS and are a different thing
       with a different cycle; see the todos-vs-beans page.

       OPEN → WORK → CLOSE (bean folio-assistant-m8gz, owner ruling
       2026-10-24, option A). Until then this diagram drew the whole
       cycle and nothing called it, while 18 other diagrams copied its
       claim, resolve and archive steps by hand and drifted: seven
       opened a bean they never closed, eight closed one without
       archiving it. The two halves are now processes of their own —
       Process_BeanOpen (bean-open.bpmn) and Process_BeanClose
       (bean-close.bpmn) — and every process that works on a bean calls
       both, as this one does. `check:bean-calls` refuses a claim,
       resolve or archive op anywhere else.

       A BEAN IS NEVER DELETED. `beans delete` exists in the CLI, which
       is exactly why the prohibition has to be written where an agent
       reads rather than left implied. Work that turns out not to be
       wanted is SCRAPPED, with its reasons (Process_BeanClose).

       TWO LAYERS, and confusing them is how a step comes to announce an
       effect it does not have. `claim`, `note`, `resolve` and `archive`
       are what the WORKFLOW ENGINE performs on a process instance's own
       bean when a step completes. Creating, scrapping and editing are the
       AGENT's own `beans` CLI calls; the engine has no op for them.
       An earlier diagram carried `<cat-harness.processes:bean action="create"/>`, which
       the engine never read — `op` is the attribute — so the step
       silently did nothing for weeks.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <bpmn:process id="Process_BeanLifecycle" name="Agent bean lifecycle" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>The whole life of a work-plan item, drawn the way every bean-touching process now runs it: OPEN the bean (check before you create, find out whose it is, claim it or leave it alone), do the work keeping the body current, then CLOSE it in a state that says why (complete and archive, scrap with reasons and archive, or record the blocker and hand back).

You are in this process the moment durable work is identified — which is before the first tool call, not after the work is done. The two halves are called processes, Process_BeanOpen and Process_BeanClose, so the rules live in one place: a process that works on a bean calls the first where the bean becomes its own and the second before each end it reaches from there.

The one irreversible thing is refused outright. Unwanted work is SCRAPPED with its reasons, never deleted, because a scrapped bean stops the next agent re-entering a dead end while a deleted one leaves a sibling unable to tell abandonment from accident.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>

    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_BeanLifecycle">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Agent (this session)" partitionElementRef="authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Owns every transition on a bean it holds. Whether the bean is its own at all is decided inside Process_BeanOpen, whose sibling lane takes someone else's bean; this lane only reads the answer at GW_Yours and stops when it is not.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_DurableWork</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanOpen</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Yours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_NotYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Work</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanClose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Recorded</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_DurableWork" name="Durable work&#10;identified"/>

    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanOpen" name="Open the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanOpen">
      <bpmn:documentation>Check before you create (exact-title search), create the bean when none exists, find out whose it is, and claim it — or leave it alone when a sibling holds it. Process_BeanOpen is the one place a claim is drawn.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="bean-coordination"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:callActivity>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Yours" name="Bean claimed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress, so work it. `not yours`: someone else holds it and nothing was written; stop here rather than resolve, scrap or edit a bean you do not own.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_NotYours" name="Not yours —&#10;left alone"/>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_Work" name="Work, keeping the body current&#10;(this is 'edit')">
      <bpmn:documentation>Editing a bean is not a separate ceremony: check off
todo items as they happen, append measurements with the command and date that
produced them, and record what you now know that the next agent does not. A
bean whose body is a title is a placeholder, not a plan.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/>
        <cat-harness.processes:bean op="note"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanClose" name="Close the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanClose">
      <bpmn:documentation>End the bean in a state that says why: done is completed and archived, not wanted is scrapped with its reasons and archived, blocked records what it waits on and goes back to `todo`. Process_BeanClose is the one place resolve and archive are drawn.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:callActivity>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Recorded" name="State recorded"/>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_1" sourceRef="Start_DurableWork" targetRef="Call_BeanOpen"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_2" sourceRef="Call_BeanOpen" targetRef="GW_Yours"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_3" name="not yours" sourceRef="GW_Yours" targetRef="End_NotYours"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_4" name="claimed" sourceRef="GW_Yours" targetRef="Task_Work"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_5" sourceRef="Task_Work" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_6" sourceRef="Call_BeanClose" targetRef="End_Recorded"/>
  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_BeanLifecycle">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_BeanLifecycle" bpmnElement="Process_BeanLifecycle">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Agent_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="940" height="260" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_DurableWork_di" bpmnElement="Start_DurableWork"><dc:Bounds x="220" y="190" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Call_BeanOpen_di" bpmnElement="Call_BeanOpen"><dc:Bounds x="315" y="148" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="GW_Yours_di" bpmnElement="GW_Yours" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="490" y="183" width="50" height="50" />
        
      <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="470" y="144" width="90" height="35" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_NotYours_di" bpmnElement="End_NotYours"><dc:Bounds x="497" y="280" width="36" height="36" />
        
      <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="537" y="280.5" width="90" height="35" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Work_di" bpmnElement="Task_Work"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="148" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Call_BeanClose_di" bpmnElement="Call_BeanClose"><dc:Bounds x="815" y="148" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_Recorded_di" bpmnElement="End_Recorded"><dc:Bounds x="1010" y="190" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_1_di" bpmnElement="BF_1">
        <di:waypoint x="256" y="208" />
        <di:waypoint x="315" y="208" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_2_di" bpmnElement="BF_2">
        <di:waypoint x="435" y="208" />
        <di:waypoint x="490" y="208" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_3_di" bpmnElement="BF_3"><di:waypoint x="515" y="233"/><di:waypoint x="515" y="280"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="519" y="247.5" width="90" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_4_di" bpmnElement="BF_4">
        <di:waypoint x="540" y="208" />
        <di:waypoint x="610" y="208" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_5_di" bpmnElement="BF_5">
        <di:waypoint x="730" y="208" />
        <di:waypoint x="815" y="208" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_6_di" bpmnElement="BF_6">
        <di:waypoint x="935" y="208" />
        <di:waypoint x="1010" y="208" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
